{% endfor %}**Proposal (Measurement and build tools)** · `proposal:devperf:tools` Accepted with measurement conditions: use cargo-nextest for structured per-test duration and execution results, with timing termination and automatic retries disabled, while retaining a separate doctest path and the claim/result join of (`rec:testing:decision`). Use sccache as a candidate for measured compiler reuse and LLVM lld as a linker candidate where supported; accept either only after like-for-like clean and incremental measurements show a benefit and preserve correctness and debugging. Cache keys must respect compiler, target, profile, features and relevant inputs; misses and waits remain visible. These tool roles are accepted, not claims of supported versions or integration. The foundation bite adopts each tool only after like-for-like measurements show a benefit, retains the separate doctest path with nextest and limits compiler caching to builds where it measurably helps. Review licences, platform support, runner capture, ignored-test coverage and secret-safe output before adopting them. Tool selection and profile experiments must not introduce network access or alter supported workload coverage by implication. A tool warning must remain separate from semantic exit status.

**Gate (Performance foundation)** · `gate:devperf:foundation` {{ require(comparison.before_bite == 1, 'performance discipline precedes domain implementation') }}In the shared foundation bite before domain bite {{ comparison.before_bite }}, join every operation/test label to its level, suite, implementation, applicable budgets, raw result and metered duration. Render and validate registry fields and references, enforce complete accounting and emit owned warnings/findings without feeding them into test or gate exit status. Probe fast and slow successful tests, fast and slow failing tests, noisy clocks, cold caches, overlapping spans, missing measurements and an exceeded admitted budget; all timing-only variations preserve the functional verdict and execution roster. Probe missing or malformed declarations as structural policy errors, distinct from duration excess. Verify no automatic retry, skip or timeout follows a budget warning, and preserve benchmark baselines and inconclusive performance evidence separately. Measure and decide dev/test profile choices, review tool proposals and disposition the initial registry candidate. The foundation implementer and repository reviewer own closure through actual test-site claims; this document mints no executed claim. The reporting mechanism is enforced from this bite, while timing is never enforced as a verdict (`rule:devperf:nonverdict`).
